"""Fixtures for the Go gateway's definitions (A-9 S4), generated by driving the Python code: a corpus of pinned definition
files through the loader's decision (agent_xrs.AgentXRs._decide, then engine.definitions.from_pin, which is engine.profile.parse
and the JSON schema), and scenarios of the loader's poll (agent_xrs.AgentXRs.poll over a real engine.dispatch.Gateway whose Core
(engine.core.Core.publish_definitions) talks to a recording HTTP server), each step recording what changed, the set that
resulted, the rows the store would hold and the exact requests the core was sent.

gateway/internal/definitions/testdata/definitions.json is read by the Go tests (definitions_python_test.go). The JSON schema
Python validates against is copied to gateway/internal/definitions/agent-definition.schema.json, which the Go validator embeds, so
the two cannot drift: this tool's --check (through tools/gen_gateway_registry.py) fails when either differs.

A case or a step may carry "go": the expectation for Go where it deliberately differs from Python, with "why". The Go test fails
on a "go" without a "why", on a request that is extra, missing or reordered, and on a "why" with no "go".
"""
